## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Firebase Project Setup Required**
> 
> You'll need to create a free Firebase project:
> 
> 1. Go to [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/)
> 2. Click "Add project" and follow the wizard
> 3. Enable **Firestore Database** (Start in test mode for now)
> 4. Go to Project Settings → General → Your apps
> 5. Click "Web" icon (</>) to register your app
> 6. Copy the Firebase configuration object
> 
> **Setup is much simpler than Google Drive** - no OAuth complexity, just paste config values!

## Cloud-Based Authentication
To satisfy the requirement of "asking ID/Password every time" and making the app work across different devices, we will:
1. **Move Auth to Cloud**: Check Firebase Firestore for the username and password hash during login.
2. **Prevent Unauthorized Setup**: Once an admin account is created globally, others cannot "Setup" a new one on the same project without the password.
3. **Session Management**: Ensure the session is secure and can be cleared if needed.

4. **Validation**: If the phrases match the stored hash in the cloud, the user will be allowed to set a new password.

## Android App (APK) Transition
To convert this web app into an Android APK, we will use **Capacitor**:
1. **Integration**: Install `@capacitor/core`, `@capacitor/cli`, and `@capacitor/android`.
2. **Setup**: Initialize Capacitor in the project and link it to the `dist` build folder.
3. **Platform Add**: Add the Android platform to the project.
4. **Build Flow**: Generate a production web build (`npm run build`), then sync it to the Android project (`npx cap sync`).
5. **APK Generation**: The final APK is created using Android Studio.

