#### [MODIFY] [App.tsx](file:///c:/Users/SONU%20MAHTO/Downloads/sonu-ice-cream-shop%20(1)/App.tsx)

**Replace Google Drive sync with Firebase & Implement Cloud Auth:**

1. **Remove `DriveSyncPanel` component** (Completed)
2. **Create [FirebaseSyncPanel](file:///c:/Users/SONU%20MAHTO/Downloads/sonu-ice-cream-shop%20%281%29/App.tsx#1274-1530) component** (Completed)

3. **Implement [handleLogin](file:///c:/Users/SONU%20MAHTO/Downloads/sonu-ice-cream-shop%20%281%29/App.tsx#167-238) with Cloud Check:**
   - First, check if the Firebase configuration exists.
   - If configured, check Firestore for a document matching the username.
   - If the user exists in Firestore, compare the password hashes.
   - If it's a match, download the [DatabaseState](file:///c:/Users/SONU%20MAHTO/Downloads/sonu-ice-cream-shop%20%281%29/types.ts#58-71) and log in.
   - This allows any shared link to work with the same credentials.

4. **Update `useEffect` for Init:**
   - On mount, check if a global "Owner" exists in Firestore (if config is present) to determine if we should show "Setup" or "Sign In".

5. **Security Enhancements (Forgot Password):**
   - Add `recoveryHash` to [DatabaseState](file:///c:/Users/SONU%20MAHTO/Downloads/sonu-ice-cream-shop%20%281%29/types.ts#58-71).
   - Update [LoginScreen](file:///c:/Users/SONU%20MAHTO/Downloads/sonu-ice-cream-shop%20%281%29/App.tsx#326-422) to handle the recovery state.
   - Implement [handleResetPassword](file:///c:/Users/SONU%20MAHTO/Downloads/sonu-ice-cream-shop%20%281%29/App.tsx#239-284) logic that verifies the recovery phrase against Firestore.

